 "description": "*AC/DC playing in background*\n\nYour typical bounty hunters thrashing...or is it?",
 "strategy": "Some stats first:\n\n-Activation (by thrid turn at latest, not including the Emperor of Mob. Points): 9\n\n-Average destiny (minus starting; Rendili, Interuption (V), Greedo and DB's pulled): 2.78\n\n-Destinies by number (notice the pimp bar graph)\n\n0's:0\n\n1's:-------------13\n\n2's:--------8\n\n3's:------------12\n\n4's:----4\n\n5's:-------7\n\n6's:--2\n\n7's:0\n\nWell, here it is, the uber bounty hunter beats.  Unfortunately, the destiny is rather low.  Fortunately, most of the stuff you'll be pulling will take away most of the 1's and 2's, and you have a lot of cards to help them anyways.\n\nPlaying is fairly easy, the tricky part is remembering what all the cards do, and pulling the right things at the right time.  First turn, pull Rendili, Coruscant: DB and Greedo.  Deploy and move to the DB to flip (hopefully no Luke yet ^_^), and peek at force and grab it if ya need it.  On following turns, get a decent-sized force togther, pull what you can, and go balls to the wall.\n\nCard selection:\n\nAs I see it, there are two do-able kinds of AOBS:  the Prepared Defense, non-Jabba version, and the Any Methods Necessary, Scum and Villainy version.  I think Prepared Defenses version is better, because it doesn't limit your options on the first turns, and allows you to react to your opponent.  Also all the effects aren't inner-dependent on each other, and they take up a lot of space.\n\n-4-LOM (non V): With four droids and a bunch of aliens, he will get big, and can be pulled by Zuckuss (V).\n\n-starships: 6 pilot slots, 7 pilots, basically all you need for any space package.\n\n-Jabba's Through: Pull my weapons, and add to a draw if I need it.\n\n-Ability x3: Only 3 characters it can't retrieve, so why not?\n\nThe matchups are basically covered in the effects section of the decklist, since it's pretty self-explainitory after then.  Any criticism/praise/donations welcome.",
